<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Mercaria by Oxy — the STATIC sitemap.

  This is the FLAG-OFF FLOOR (#75), the sibling of robots.txt beside it. When
  SEO_ROUTES_ENABLED is on, the worker proxies /sitemap.xml to the API, which
  renders an index over four paginated collections with a real per-entity
  lastmod. This copy is what a crawler gets when that lookup cannot answer, so
  it advertises the home page and nothing else: a build-time catalogue listing
  would be a second sitemap authority, stale from the moment it was written,
  and it could not apply the indexability policy at all.

  The modification date is FIXED and edited by hand (#371). A generator used to
  stamp it with the build date, which dirtied this tracked file on every build
  and told crawlers that every page changed on whatever day somebody happened
  to run one. Deriving it from the last commit touching the home screen is no
  better — the most recent such commit removed type casts and changed nothing a
  reader sees. Edit it when the home page's content actually changes; the
  protocol also allows dropping the element entirely if no honest value exists.

  packages/backend/src/services/seo/__tests__/seo-sitemap-static.test.ts parses
  this file and fails the build when it drifts from the public route registry,
  when the date is unreadable or in the future, or when a build step starts
  regenerating it again.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://mercaria.co/</loc>
    <lastmod>2026-07-07</lastmod>
    <changefreq>daily</changefreq>
    <priority>1</priority>
  </url>
</urlset>